<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhao Tuo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 137 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhao Tuo was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> general sent to conquer the far south who founded the kingdom of Nanyue, with its capital at Panyu (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangzhou">Guangzhou</a>), in 204 BCE. Ruling Chinese settlers and Yue peoples, he adopted local customs, accepted Han overlordship in 196 BCE and later styled himself emperor. He is said to have reigned for some seventy years before his death in 137 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zhao-tuo.jpg" alt="Zhao Tuo" width="320" height="517" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Chen (Iamdavidtheking 11:50, 10 September 2007 (UTC)) · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_statue_of_Zhao_Tuo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
